# JavaScript Projects

A collection of small JavaScript exercises and projects that I build while learning JavaScript.

This repository is mainly for practice, problem-solving, and tracking my progress as I learn.

## Projects

### Faulty Calculator

A simple JavaScript learning exercise based on a faulty calculator.

The calculator performs the wrong operation about 10% of the time:

- `+` becomes `-`
- `-` becomes `/`
- `*` becomes `+`
- `/` becomes `**`

The other 90% of the time, it performs the normal operation.

### Concepts Practiced

- `prompt()`
- `Number()`
- `Math.random()`
- `if / else if / else`
- Basic arithmetic operators
- Conditional logic

## Note

This is a small learning exercise, not a production-ready calculator application.
